# .TODO

Next step for the ci/cd workflow in this directory.

## full build (next step)

Status: ci.yml gates a lite build only (core library plus stb, nanosvg, zxing)
on debian trixie and arch, running the no service tests. couchbase, sdl3, haru,
and drogon are left out of that gate to keep it offline and fast.

Next fix (add a full build, likely a nightly or manual job, not the merge gate):
- sdl3: install the system dev libraries it links against per distro (x11,
  wayland, alsa, pulseaudio, and friends).
- haru: install libpng and zlib dev.
- couchbase: it still downloads at configure time, so make it offline first:
  - commit a CPM source cache and point CPM_SOURCE_CACHE at it. the packages are
    snappy, spdlog, gsl, hdr_histogram, llhttp, taocpp-json (with pegtl), asio.
  - commit a cacert.pem and use it instead of fetching from curl.se.
- drogon: optional. needs a PIC build (see the root .TODO shared library item)
  when the shared library is also wanted. the communication path and
  test_communication_smtps depend on it.
- databases: test_database_couchbase_rw and test_database_scylla_rw need a
  running service, so keep them out of an unattended gate or stand up a service
  container.
